   "text": "I read the image as two separate capreomycin-type cyclic peptides, so the SMILES has two fragments joined by a dot. I assigned the stereochemistry by hand from the wedges and hashes. One uncertainty: for the bottom molecule's ring-bearing \u03b1-carbon, I assumed the wedge's narrow end sits at the stereocentre.\n\n**Top molecule (Ser-type ring):**\n- The macrocycle runs through a ureido-dehydroalanine, a residue with a CH\u2082NH side chain, a serine, a 2,3-diaminopropionic acid and a cyclic guanidine residue.\n- The side chain on the CH\u2082NH is a \u03b2-lysine unit: C(=O)CH\u2082CH(NH\u2082)CH\u2082CH\u2082CH\u2082NH\u2082.\n- The cyclic guanidine is a 2-amino-tetrahydropyrimidine ring.\n- The ureido C=C is drawn with the ureido N trans to the ring NH, which I wrote as E.\n\n**Bottom molecule:**\n- It has the same skeleton, but the serine CH\u2082OH is replaced by CH\u2083, giving an alanine residue.\n- The ureido C=C geometry is drawn the same way as in the top molecule.\n\nI worked out the CIP configuration at each stereocentre from the drawing and converted it to @/@@ for the atom order in my SMILES. The result is S at every stereocentre except the cyclic guanidine ring carbon, which is R, in both molecules.\n\nSMILES: NC(=O)N/C=C1/NC(=O)[C@@H](CNC(=O)C[C@@H](N)CCCN)NC(=O)[C@@H](CO)NC(=O)[C@H](N)CNC(=O)[C@@H]([C@H]2CCN=C(N)N2)NC1=O.NC(=O)N/C=C1/NC(=O)[C@@H](CNC(=O)C[C@@H](N)CCCN)NC(=O)[C@@H](C)NC(=O)[C@H](N)CNC(=O)[C@@H]([C@H]2CCN=C(N)N2)NC1=O"
